interaction.md
### Feedback view

| State | Entry or trigger | What the user sees | Words | Actions with key | Exit |
| Default | `/<org>/<ws>/feedback/<n>` | header (breadcrumb, title, number, status, flags, Previous/Next, More), version tabs, toolbar (Compare, Draw on Screenshot, zoom), screenshot with references and the anchor outline, right panel (Thread · Details), footer composer and review buttons | acceptance line, e.g. "Not reviewed yet" | R, A, ⇧R, V, S, C, D, [ ], J/K, Esc | list |
| Loading | | header skeleton, image placeholder at the screenshot's ratio, thread skeleton | | | |
| Image loading | | thumbnail blurred up to the full image | | | |
| Image failed | signed URL fails | in the image area | "Couldn't load the screenshot. The feedback and thread are fine. Try again." | Try Again | |
| Compare | C | two panes with version Selects; linked zoom and pan; references on both; the footer acts on the right pane and its label names that version | "Compare" toggle pressed | C or Esc exits | |
| Drawing | D (desktop) | toolbar over the image; marks join the draft comment; composer shows "{n} marks" | | C, 1–7, ⌘Z, Esc | |
| Composing | R or click the field | composer grows; Comment becomes primary; the context line above it reads "On v{n} {kind}" | placeholder "Comment on v{n}…" | ⌘↩ sends, Esc leaves the field | |
| Request Changes, no text | ⇧R with an empty composer | composer focused with the prompt; context line "Requesting changes on v{n}" with × (back to a plain comment, text kept) | placeholder "What should change in v{n}?" · button "Request Changes" | ⌘↩ | |
| Implementation awaiting review | status Implemented, v{n} shown (the default version while one awaits review, VF-2) | Approve v{n} is the primary | "Approve v{n}" | A | |
| Original of a change request | v0 shown, kind Change Request | Approve is not offered (nobody can approve v0 of a change request); Comment is the primary; Request Changes stays | | R, ⇧R | |
| Original of a Comment-kind feedback | v0 shown, kind Comment | "Approve v0" accepts the feedback (owner-decisions.md #26) | "Approve v0" | A | |
| Mockup or alternative, decision open | a mockup or alternative shown while a decision request is open | the button names what it ends | "Approve v{n} and Close Decision" | A | |
| Approve not available | an older implementation, a version already accepted, or one you approved | Approve `aria-disabled` with the reason | "v{m} is newer. Review that one." · "v{n} is already accepted." · "You approved v{n}. Withdraw it from your entry's More." | | |
| Approved, Undo window | any Approve (button, A, ⌘K, phone) | the approval shows at once; toast for 8 s | "Approved v{n}." · Undo | ⌘Z or Undo | Undo removes the approval and all it caused: acceptance, Decided, the decision's close, the move to Done (VF-1) |
| Change status (member) | the header status Chip, S, Footer More or ⌘K "Change Status" | Dropdown: Open, In Progress, Implemented; Accepted shown `aria-disabled` | "Change Status (S)" · "Accepted comes from an Approve on the implementation." | ↑/↓, ↩, Esc | A33: "he changes the state of the specific comment/comments" |
| Status changed by hand | a member picks a status | chip changes; thread line; toast with Undo. In Progress reads "In Progress · {name}". Implemented adds "v{n} Implementation · marked by {name}" with no screenshot (the canvas shows the previous one with a line) and sends the review requests; acceptance still follows Approve and Request Changes | "{name} changed the status to {status}." · "Moved #{n} to {list}." · Undo · "No after-screenshot. {name} marked this implemented by hand." | ⌘Z or Undo within 8 s | an audit event records each manual change |
| Accepted, status locked | status Accepted | status control `aria-disabled` | "Request changes on v{n} to reopen it." | | |
| Accepted | | status chip Accepted; acceptance line names approvers. On an accepted mockup or alternative the line reads "Decided · approved by {names}" instead (VF-24) | "Accepted · approved by {names}" | | |
| Objection open | | acceptance line | "{n} objection open · {name}: “{first line}”" | | |
| Decision open | | decision card at the top of the thread; Vote primary in the card if you haven't voted | | V | |
| Question open | | flag Needs Answer; the question entry has Answer Question, which puts the composer in answer mode: context line "Answering {name}'s question" with ×, send button "Answer Question" | | | |
| Claimed | In Progress | header line | "In Progress · {name} via {client}" | Unclaim (More) | |
| Claim refused (shown to people) | copilot tried while flagged | thread entry | "{name} via {client} couldn't claim this: it needs an answer first." | | |
| Empty thread | no entries | one line in the thread | "No comments yet." | | |
| Guest | role guest | Approve and Request Changes shown, `aria-disabled`, with the reason; Comment and Vote stay; Footer More shows Draw on Screenshot only; the status Chip is read-only (A31: comment, draw, vote) | "Guests can comment, draw and vote. Approving and requesting changes need a member." | | |
| Live | others act | new entries append; "2 new" pill if scrolled up; header chip changes with a thread line "Status changed to Implemented by Ben via Claude" | | | |
| Newer version while drafting | a version is posted while your composer holds text for an older one | inline note above the composer | "v{n} was just posted. Your comment will go on v{old}." | Move to v{n} | |
| Pending write | your entry sending | entry shows at once, a quiet clock icon | | | |
| Failed write | entry fails | entry stays with an inline error | "Couldn't post your comment. Snapmark had a problem. Your text is kept. Try again." | Try Again, Delete | |
| Offline | | review buttons and Comment `aria-disabled` with reason; composer stays usable (draft) | "Offline. Your comment is kept here and can be sent when you're back." | | |
| Not found or no access | | 404 page | "This feedback doesn't exist, or you don't have access." | Go to Inbox | |
| Deleted by you | Header More › Delete Feedback | back to the `from` list (else the list for its status) with the Undo toast | "Deleted #{n}." · Undo | ⌘Z or Undo within 8 s | list |
| Phone | < 640 px | Phone feedback view (below) | | | |

conformance.md
## Design system

| Area | Departure | Impact | Fix |
| Brand blue literal | screens.md:16 names `#2492FF` for `accent`. The pinned token is `#0f72db` (`tokens.css:142`), and white on `#2492FF` is 3.17:1. A ACC-3: "Text reaches 4.5:1 against its background". The Mac editor already notes "4.7:1, where #2492ff is 3.2:1". | Medium. A builder who copies the hex fails contrast on every primary button. | Name the token only (`accent`), never the hex, in screens.md:16 and the design-system.md note. **Fixed in spec.** screens.md names the token `accent` only. |
| `info` blue | DS `tabs.md`: the chosen tab keeps "a 2 px underline in the `info` colour"; elements table (interaction.md:618) lights the current page with `info`; `--ds-color-info` is `blue-600`. Brief No-Go: "No blue outlines, borders, icons, links or labels". screens.md:642 says the bar is neutral. | Medium. Two hues of blue, and three statements about the current-page mark. | Decide that Snapmark's `info` is neutral for tabs, chosen state and "is" chips, and write that in `examples/snapmark.md`. **Fixed in spec.** screens.md How to read and interaction.md Elements: the current page and chosen tab use a neutral mark. The same line goes into `examples/snapmark.md` when the kit is set up. |
| Button variants | Spec: "primary, default, light, danger" (screens.md:25). DS `button.md`: Primary, Secondary, Outlined, Ghost, Icon button, Text link; "Don't make a destructive button a loud red fill". Used for Delete Workspace (screens.md:1361) and Leave Organisation (screens.md:1459). | Low. Four names for three roles; `danger` invites a red fill. | default = Secondary, light = Ghost, danger = Outlined with the `pass` tone; rename in the wrapper. **Fixed in spec.** secondary, ghost, outlined + `pass` in screens.md's inventory and every Controls table. |
| Chip, badge, status chip | One `Chip` serves status, flag, kind, Guest and filter (screens.md:42). DS `badge-chip.md`: "Badge: a state the thing is in" (inert), "Chip: a fact about a thing, often clickable", "Not a Badge with a prop to make it a Chip." | Medium. Status, flags and Guest would be clickable-looking. | Split into Chip (filters, toggles), Badge (status, flags, Guest, kind) and StatusChip (header facts); a Badge is never a button. **Fixed in spec.** Chip (filters) and Badge (states, inert) in screens.md's inventory. |
| Tabs for filters | See Interaction model. | Medium | Chip toggles and a segmented control. **Fixed in spec.** See Interaction model. |
| Breadcrumbs and Back link | See Interaction model. | Low | Back link. **For owner** (owner-decisions.md #13). |
| Bars | DS `bars.md`: "Footer: one line under every screen" with the shortcut entry; HeroUI `Navbar` is "not app chrome". The spec has no footer, builds AppShell from Listbox and Dropdown, and the DrawingToolbar from "Button group, Tooltip". | Low. Roving focus and More Actions overflow are not specified for the DrawingToolbar. | Build the toolbar on React Aria `Toolbar` (one Tab stop, arrows); record "no footer" as an exception. Toolbar: **Fixed in spec.** DrawingToolbar on React Aria Toolbar (screens.md inventory). No footer: **For owner** (owner-decisions.md #13). |
| Tooltips on touch | DS `touch-and-responsive.md` section 3. Tables "drop rank-3 columns into Tooltips" (screens.md:2453) and the version tab's kind, author, date and PR sit in a Tooltip (interaction.md:624). | Low. Facts a phone user cannot reach. | Put them in the row dialog or a Details line on touch. **Fixed in spec.** screens.md Layout checks ("Facts on touch"); interaction.md Elements (version tab). |
| Control sizes and text | 32 / 40 / 48, radius 8 and 12, text 16, hit areas 32 and 44 (screens.md:17) | Pass. Matches `foundations/owner-decisions.md`. | none |
| Light and dark | WEB-28: follow the system | Pass. | none |
| Colour roles | Tally bars neutral, status never colour alone (screens.md:1156) | Pass. | none |
| Zoom cap | 150 % checked against a 130 % cap (screens.md:18) | Pass (stricter than the system). | none |
| Case | See Words, case row. | Medium | Owner decision. **For owner** (owner-decisions.md #19). Title Case default applied. |

## Component inventory

Status uses the plan's three words, not screens.md's ("new variant", "missing", "have"):

- **exists**: a HeroUI v3 component used as-is behind a thin wrapper; the look comes only from the `snapmark-kit/packages/tokens` HeroUI theme.
- **adapt**: a HeroUI component that needs a Snapmark variant; the row names the tokens and props.
- **new**: a Snapmark component with no HeroUI base, composed from the parts above.

**Counts: 18 exists, 15 adapt, 33 new** (66 web and extension components), plus 4 Mac surfaces and the pieces that move from the Mac app into `snapmark-kit/packages/annotations` and `packages/redaction`. Feature dialogs (Request a Decision, Post Version, Set Up the Extension, Invite People, Add Module, Seats) are put together from the rows below and are not counted on their own.

**Callers today: 0 for every web and extension row.** `snapmark-kit` does not exist, `snapmark-web/` and `snapmark-chrome/` hold one `README.md` each, and no `package.json` in the repo lists `@heroui`. "Called by" lists the screens.md screens whose Controls, Components or Filters tables use the component, and the interaction.md state tables for Skeleton, Spinner and Toast. The first screen built becomes the first caller.

**Paths.** Generic parts go in `snapmark-kit/packages/ui/src/<Name>.tsx`. The canvas and toolbar go in `snapmark-kit/packages/annotations/src/react/<Name>.tsx`, so `ui` does not pull in Fabric. Web-only parts go in `snapmark-web/src/features/<feature>/components/<Name>.tsx` (design 11). Extension-only parts go in `snapmark-chrome/src/components/<Name>.tsx`. A part used by both web and extension goes in the kit, because apps never import from each other (design 11).

**Assumption, not checked:** the HeroUI v3 names below (TextField, ComboBox for Autocomplete, NumberField, Toast) come from the spec and from memory, not from the v3 catalogue. Check them when the kit is set up in milestone 1.


